RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7688912Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7700600Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7818660Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7831775Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7832876Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7833516Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7833842Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7834537Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7835321Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7835747Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7836007Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7836567Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7836821Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7837336Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7838091Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7838710Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7839213Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7839393Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7839546Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7839794Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7839982Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7840352Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7840487Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7840588Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7840734Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7841010Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7841736Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7842047Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7842501Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7842694Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7842953Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7843497Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7843888Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7844452Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7844829Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7845195Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7845781Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7846322Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7863937Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7864809Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7877995Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7878778Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7879289Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7879934Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7880502Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7903333Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7904158Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7915383Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7916134Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7916524Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7916708Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7916875Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7917115Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T22:11:20.7917293Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
